cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ORION: Guiding RL with LLM Plans for Multi-Domain Slice Placement"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mayaleh
    given-names: Mahmoud S.
    affiliation: "Conservatoire national des arts et metiers"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-17"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mahmoudmayaleh/ORION-v1"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  ORION admits and places 6G network slices across federated administrative domains. A
  language model turns an operator intent into a structured slice specification and an
  abstract placement plan over domains. A PPO-trained Multi-Domain Orchestrator decides
  admission and partitions that plan across domains from per-domain aggregates rather
  than full substrate state, and behaviour-cloned per-domain actors place the assigned
  VNFs on concrete nodes inside their own domain. The repository contains the system,
  its test suite and the experiment entry points.
keywords:
  - network-slicing
  - 6G
  - multi-domain-orchestration
  - reinforcement-learning
  - large-language-models
  - multi-agent-ppo
  - service-function-chaining
